course: dictionary
lesson: 5377
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The words around them tell you which meaning fits. Kneecap is one of these words. «The kneecap protects the front of the knee and helps the thigh muscles pull.» You can protect a bone, and muscles pull on bones, so here kneecap means a bone.
explain: Look for clues. «Sam wore knee pads so his kneecaps were protected when he went skating.» Knee pads are worn to keep the body safe, so this kneecap is the bone at the front of the knee.
explain: The other meaning is rare and violent. In history or news, to kneecap someone means to shoot or hurt their knee as a cruel punishment. Clues like gangs, threats or punishment tell you this meaning. Check by putting your meaning into the sentence. If it does not fit, try the other meaning.
fact: A kneecap is the small, flat, roundish bone at the front of your knee.
fact: Scientists call the kneecap the patella. It protects the knee joint.
fact: «In babies the kneecap is soft cartilage that turns to bone over the first years.»
fact: Knee pads protect kneecaps when you skate or play in goal.
fact: To kneecap someone is a rare, violent meaning: to shoot or hurt their knee as a cruel punishment. You will mostly meet it in history or news.
exercise: «The kneecap protects the front of the knee.» What is a kneecap? | *The small, flat, roundish bone at the front of your knee | A muscle in your thigh | A soft pad you wear to skate | A hard shoe for climbing
exercise: «Sam wore knee pads to protect his kneecaps when he went skating.» What do the knee pads protect? | *Your kneecaps | Your ears | Your toes | Your hair
exercise: «The gang threatened to kneecap him as a punishment.» What does kneecap mean here? | To give a knee massage | To tie a bandage around the knee | To bend the knee in prayer | *To shoot or hurt someone's knee as a cruel punishment
test: «In babies the kneecap is soft cartilage that turns to bone over the first years.» What is the proper science name for the kneecap? | Thigh | Tendon | Cartilage | *Patella
test: «A sore bump just below the kneecap in sporty children of about 10 to 15 is often Osgood-Schlatter.» What causes the sore bump in Osgood-Schlatter? | A rash on the skin | A bruise from a ball | *A tendon pulling on a growing spot of the shin bone | A broken kneecap
exam: Which sentence uses kneecap to mean the bone at the front of the knee? | «The gang vowed to kneecap their rival as a punishment.» | «The kneecap was a cheap sweet from the shop.» | *«The kneecap protects the front of the knee.»
